From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:18:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] iommu/apple-dart: Support T6050's boot-locked display
 DARTs

On the M5 Ultra Mac Studio (J775D) the boot loader leaves every display
DART locked on its own page tables. apple-dart now keeps the firmware's
mappings there and maps Linux's beside them, so the display co-processor
can be adopted with no DART fault.

On T6050 the boot loader leaves every display DART locked on its own
four-level roots (dart-dcpextN stream 23, dart-dispextN streams 0 and
16), with no reserved-table handoff. That is the case fw_mirror already
covers on T6041, T8140 and T8142: firmware's root slots are kept and
Linux maps only into the slots it owns. Add apple,t6050-dart to that
list.

Only the bare-metal apple-dart driver reads this; an APIF guest's DARTs
(apple,dart-apif) are a separate driver and unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit b379d8d8a19288ad800724d94f6699b93c9be720)
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 1234b4a771e7..e9667e8a3d41 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -4494,9 +4494,14 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		dart->locked = apple_dart_is_locked(dart);
 	/* Reserved table-page lifetime requires the matched three-level loader. */
 	dart->fw_handoff = apple_dart_fw_handoff_enabled(dart);
-	/* Preserve our retained-root path when no reserved-table handoff exists. */
+	/*
+	 * Preserve our retained-root path when no reserved-table handoff exists.
+	 * T6050's boot loader leaves every display DART locked on four-level
+	 * roots of its own (dart-dcpextN SID 23, dart-dispextN SIDs 0 and 16).
+	 */
 	dart->fw_mirror = dart->locked && !dart->fw_handoff &&
 		(of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6041-dart") ||
+		 of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6050-dart") ||
 		 of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8140-dart") ||
 		 of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8142-dart"));
 	/*
